# This agent supports two LLM backends. Configure one of the following:
#
# Option 1 — Bring your own Foundry model (BYOK, default):
#   Set FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT and AZURE_AI_MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME.
#   No GITHUB_TOKEN needed — authenticates via Managed Identity.
#   FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT is auto-injected when deployed as a hosted agent
#   (set it here only for local runs).
#
# Option 2 — GitHub Copilot model (quickest start, no Azure resources needed):
#   Comment out the Foundry vars below and set GITHUB_TOKEN to a fine-grained
#   PAT with "Copilot Requests → Read-only".
#   Create one at: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#   Classic tokens (ghp_) are not supported — use github_pat_, gho_, or ghu_ tokens.
#
# If both are set, the Foundry model takes precedence.

# GITHUB_TOKEN=
FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT=https://<account>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project>
AZURE_AI_MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME=gpt-5.4-mini

# Optional — session ID for persistence/resume across restarts. When hosted,
# the platform supplies the session id per request; set this only for local
# multi-run experiments where you want a stable, resumable session.
# FOUNDRY_AGENT_SESSION_ID=

# Optional local crash-simulation hook (see README "Testing crash recovery").
# When set to a non-negative integer N, the agent hard-crashes (os._exit(1))
# right after the Nth streamed event is checkpointed, so a restart exercises
# the resume_session() recovery path. Leave unset in production.
# SIMULATE_CRASH_AFTER_EVENTS=
